#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_negative

#% text
# `is_negative(x)` gives `true` when `x` is a negative real, `false` when it is known not to be, and stays unevaluated when neither is decided.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numbers and closed numeric expressions are decided by numerical bounds; symbols by the assumptions in force.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_negative(-3)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_negative(2.5)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_negative(3 - pi)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_negative(x)
#% output
#= is_negative(x)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Decided by assumptions:

#% cell
assuming(x < 0, is_negative(x^3))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
assuming(x < 0, is_negative(x^2))
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `is_negative(x)` is `is_positive(-x)`:

#% cell
[is_negative(log(1/2)), is_positive(-log(1/2))]
#% output
#= [true, true]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_positive`, `is_nonnegative`, `sign`
